    "narrative": "Our core offensive strategy today centers on capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Junk, who shoulders a 4.51 xERA. **Bryce Harper** (74.59) and **Lawrence Butler** (72.31) emerge as our premier options, with **Harper** offering the highest floor due to his elite 0.389 xwOBA and a strong #3 order placement that maximizes his RBI potential. Similarly, **Justin Crawford** (62.05) and **Luis Arraez** (64.92) benefit significantly from the match-up; **Crawford** is of particular interest as our primary speed threat, with his sprint speed metrics allowing us to aggressively target the scarce stolen base category despite his lower-order placement. We are also high on **Jonathan Aranda** (66.40), whose dynamic platoon edge against a right-handed arm like Young makes him a high-efficiency start in the 1B slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Gavin Sheets** (40.99), who remains on the bubble due to a sub-optimal matchup against McLean (3.49 xERA). While **Sheets** provided a decent floor, his lack of stolen base utility and the difficulty of finding a path to production against a high-skill pitcher pushed him into the reserve role behind more favorable platoon-advantaged bats. We are monitoring **Masyn Winn** (60.12) and **JJ Bleday** (48.32) closely as both carry a 32% rain risk; while **Winn** is currently cleared to start thanks to his unique combination of speed and a favorable matchup against Lowder, we are prepared to pivot if the weather forecast deteriorates further. Conversely, **Braden Montgomery** (44.51) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Imanaga, as his power profile serves as a necessary hedge against our heavy reliance on contact-oriented hitters like **Arraez**.",
